window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["vw/beetle-5c"]={"beetle-5c-activate-bluetooth-on-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth on the RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Not all RNS-315 are equipped with a Bluetooth module.</strong> </p>\n<figure><table><thead><tr><td>Module compatibility list</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3C0 035 279</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 A</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 B</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 C</td><td>Yes (conditional)</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 D</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 E</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 F</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 G</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 H</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 J</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 K</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>You can also remove the RNS 315 from its slot to check. Behind it, you’ll find a label with the RNS-315’s MAC address.<br/>If the MAC address contains only zeros (MAC: 00:00:00:00:00:00), your RNS-315 is not equipped with the Bluetooth module. </p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns_315_j_mac_non-6328b9e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns315_mac_oui-eed1a386.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>3</strong><br/>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck the “Telephone Transceiver inactive” box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS315_3C0-035-279_Module37_Byte3-74e93c9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-comfort-turn-signals":"<p><strong>Function:</strong> Activates the convenience turn signals.  </p>\n<p><em>(By default, the number of flashes is 3. You can change this value to any number between 1 and 5.) </em>)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on<strong> “Coding – 07” </strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte<strong> 12: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check <strong>“Comfort Turn Signals active</strong> ”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte12-011f47aa.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-coming-home-leaving-home":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>To activate Coming-Home / Leaving-Home.  </p>\n<p>(To work properly, the vehicle must be equipped with a light sensor. Headlight switch must be in “Auto” position.   <br/>Without the light sensor, it will be necessary to make a headlight call to activate the coming-home).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>10 </strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Leaving-Home (LH) active”<br/>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-polo-6r-cominghome-b8af74dc.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the daytime running lights (DRL).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>23</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6 : </strong> Check Function “Daytime Running Light (DRL)” active</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte23-e94f1178.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12 </strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Tick “Daytime Running Light (DRL) adjustable (Manually AND/OR instrument Cluster)”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte12-2c0d5984.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-driving-school-mode-rcd-210-rcd-310":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to add a Driving School mode view to the RCD 210, RCD 310 that displays turn signals, speed … (Also ideal for accompanied driving) <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“56 – Radio</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Channel 2</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“1</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/golf6_golf_vi_fahrschulfunktion-5b883ac1.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-hidden-menu-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the hidden menu in RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Developer mode (temporary)</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong><em>Enabled</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart RNS 315.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-035-279_Module37_Adaptation_Developer_mode_tem-59109da4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-hidden-menu-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the hidden menu in RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 50</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1T0-035-680-C_Module37_Adaptation_Channel50-1a7d6a90.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-interior-lighting-when-key-is-removed":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to activate the interior lighting when the key is removed from the neiman.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>12</strong>:<br/>Bit<strong> 2</strong>: check “Interior Light after ignition Key removal active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte12-2c0d5984.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-off-road-mode-on-discover-pq":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add Offroad mode to Discover PQ with navigation.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-compass_0x15</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass_over-threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Restart the Discover Media PQ (hold down the ON/OFF button for at least 5 seconds).</p>\n<p>Depending on your hardware and firmware, the off-road menu may appear directly in the Menu, or it may be hidden:<br/>Press the VOICE-MENU-NAV buttons to access the secret menu, where you’ll now find the OFFROAD screen:  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadpq-1024x768-39023fd7.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadmenupq-1024x619-dc3e8b4c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroad-1024x631-441bee99.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-activate-rain-sensor":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the rain sensor.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “Long Coding Helper” :</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select,</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14</strong>: </em> <br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Sensor Function active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte14-cd640f80.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2: </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “RLS” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em><em>Byte <strong>4</strong>: </em> </em><br/><em><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck “Rain Sensor inactive”.</em></em></p>","beetle-5c-activate-rns-510-voice-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate voice control on the RNS 510 (SDS).  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:</strong> RNS 510 firmware must be version v2660.</p>\n<p>Activating voice control brings up the “Voice control” menu in the RNS 510’s SETUP menu.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>3</strong>, check the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Microphone Diagnostics active</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>7</strong>, uncheck the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Voice Control inactive</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS510_Menu_Commande_Vocale-bf5955d7.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>To install the microphone, connect the microphone lead to the rear of the RNS 510. Connect to pins (Mic-)C1 and (Mic+)C7. </p>","beetle-5c-activate-wiper-change-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates changeover mode for front wipers.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “Long Coding Helper” :</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select,</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 2</strong>: Check “Service Position for Front Wiper active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte14-cd640f80.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2: </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 23</strong>: <em>Set value to 1.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Adaptation_channel231-91e9521d.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-adjust-light-sensor-sensitivity":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Adjusts the sensitivity of the light sensor.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>:  </em><br/><em>Bits <strong>3–4</strong>: Select from the drop-down list<br/>– 00 Normal light activation threshold<br/>– 08 Earlier light activation threshold (+20%)<br/>– 10 Light Activation Threshold earlier (+40%)<br/>– 08 Light Activation Threshold earlier (+60%)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-automatic-closing-of-windows-and-roof-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Automatically closes windows and sunroof when it rains.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “Long Coding Helper” :</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6: </strong> Check “Rain closing active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4A6D5E39-CE5A-476F-995D-444CD637E3AD-af64c8a6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 </strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “RLS” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2: </strong> Check “Rain closing active”.</em></p>","beetle-5c-automatic-door-locking-after-30s":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set automatic door unlocking when the vehicle has been unlocked but no doors have been opened for 30 seconds.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck “Central Locking Re-locking (after 30 seconds) active”.</em><em><br/></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte4-6c468b48.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-automatic-door-locks":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Auto-Lock (Automatic Locking above 15 km/h)”.</em><em><br/></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte0-87553eca.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-automatic-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to configure automatic door unlocking when the ignition key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock (Unlocking when Removing the Ignition Key)”.</em><em><br/></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte0-87553eca.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-automatic-headlamp-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-automatic-headlight-activation-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit<strong> 1 </strong>: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-change-number-of-flashes-comfort-flashers":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the number of flashes after activating the comfort indicators.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on<strong> “Adaptation – 10” </strong></p>\n<p>5 – Select<strong> Channel 43</strong> (Lights: Comfort Turn Signals (Cycles) from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value between 1 and 5</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Adaptation_channel43-3a96f44b.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-change-odb-language":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Select the language of your on-board computer.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Language Version</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select language from second value list  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/886F4702-2DBC-4C30-8716-D4D05CCE1338-da4cd84c.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-change-the-rcd-rns-510-theme":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the display theme of the RCD 510 and RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” for RNS510 and “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” for RCD510.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>4-5</strong>: Select from 3 themes</em><br/><em>“00 Display Variant: Highline</em><br/><em>“10 Display Variant: Sportsline</em><br/><em>“20 Display Variant: Premium</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/69C76009-6EC7-465A-A676-8E39BA840A6B-6689b9e0.webp\"/><figcaption>Highline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3A58F148-9FBB-4DD8-BF05-E03A5351E3A8-e9b6cb9b.webp\"/><figcaption>Sportsline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4894A3B7-2ED2-4A75-9D46-CA3BFCF5A76C-8fb8de15.webp\"/><figcaption>Premium</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD / RNS 510 must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","beetle-5c-change-the-rcd-rns-ops-image":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the vehicle image of the OPS (parking aid) on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Encoding 07</strong>,” then ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose Byte<strong> 6</strong> or <strong>9</strong></p>\n<p><em>Select the vehicle from the drop-down menu:</em><br/><br/>00 = via CAN<br/>01 = Polo 6R<br/>02 = New Beetle<br/>03 = New Beetle Cabrio<br/>04 = Scirocco<br/>05 = Golf 5<br/>06 = Jetta<br/>07 = Golf 6 Variant<br/>08 = Golf 6 Cabrio<br/>09 = Touran<br/>0A = Golf Plus<br/>0C = Tiguan<br/>0D = Sharan<br/>0E = EOS<br/>0F = Passat 3C<br/>10 = Passat Limousine<br/>11 = Passat Variant<br/>13 = Caddy<br/>14 = T5<br/>2C = Skoda Octavia<br/>2D = Skoda Octavia Kombi<br/>2E = Skoda Superb Kombi</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0864-978ed9ed.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD or RNS must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","beetle-5c-coming-leaving-home-with-fog-lamps":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables fog lamps to be used for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>13</strong>:<br/>Bit<strong> 6</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home (CH) / Leaving-Home (LH) Variant (0 = Fog Lights / 1 = Low Beam)”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte13-092427d2.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-coming-leaving-home-with-xenons":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Allows xenon (or halogen) lights to be used for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>13</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) / Leaving-Home (LH) Variant (0 = Fog Lights / 1 = Low Beam)”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte13-092427d2.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-corner-lights":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to turn on the cornering lights along with the fog lights.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on<strong> “Coding – 07” </strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 12: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Check <strong>“Turn/Cornering Lights</strong> installed/active”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte12-011f47aa.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-corner-lights-with-turn-signal":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the cornering lights to turn on along with the fog lights when the turn signal is activated.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on<strong> “Coding – 07” </strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>21: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check <strong>“Cornering/Turn Lights via Turn Signal active</strong> ”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte21-023ebd48.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-deactivate-mirrorlink":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable or remove MirrorLink from App-Connect on the MIB Discover PQ. The MirrorLink service has not been natively available on Android since June 1, 2020. For a direct connection to Android Auto.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicle configuration-Mirror_link</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Disabled</strong>” and confirm.</p>","beetle-5c-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>2: </strong>“<strong>Washer Fluid warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>1: </strong>“<strong>Seatbelt warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-delete-odb-error-led-license-plate-light":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Eliminates the error on the ODB when replacing original license plate light bulbs with non-error LEDs.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong> Coding – 07 </strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 11 </strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Uncheck “</em>Lamp diagnotics for Lisense Plate Light active<em>”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte11-e6e5cf22.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-dimming-leds-with-turn-signals":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Maintains the brightness of the LEDs (DRLs) when the turn signals are on.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Bytes <strong>23</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>7: </strong> This is a hidden bit; you must replace the 0 with a 1 directly in “Binary” (the eighth 0 with a 1)</p>","beetle-5c-disable-am-frequency-on-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable the AM radio frequency on the Discover PQ (the AM radio frequency is rarely used, unlike the FM radio frequency). <br/><em><em>For Beetle Facelift after 2015 (Radio screen like Golf 7). </em></em> </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>14</strong></p>\n<p>Set bit <strong>1</strong> <strong>“AM_disable</strong></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>","beetle-5c-disable-bluetooth-connection-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Disables the beep when a device successfully connects to the car radio’s Bluetooth.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“77 – Telephone</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select “Bluetooth acknowledgement signal” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Select <strong>“Off” </strong>from the second drop-down list</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/7P6-035-730-C_Module77_Adaptation_Bluetooth_acknow-580a5d47.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-disable-horn-without-ignition":"<p><br/><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the horn when the ignition is off.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07”</strong> then <strong>“Long Coding Helper”.</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte <strong>17</strong>, Bit <strong>3</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Check <strong>“Horn with” Terminal 15 OFF “inactive</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8B27B62E-B23B-4D69-A15C-C56C9A00FC14-c93db85d.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-disable-parking-aid-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the beep when reverse gear is engaged or when parking assistance is activated manually.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “10-Parking<strong>Assistance.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on<strong> “Adaptation – 10” </strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>“Parking Aid Activation Tone</em> ” from the drop-down list<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><em>Select <strong>“Off” from </strong>the second drop-down list</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-919-475-B_Module10_Adaptation_Parking_aid_acti-4dbee393.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-beep-horn":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set confirmation of door locking/unlocking with beep (alarm) or horn.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>5</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Tick “Acoustical Locking Confirmation (Horn) active”.</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Tick “Acoustical Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) active”. </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Tick “Anti-Theft-System Activation Acoustical Confirmation (Horn) active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte5-90daaa01.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-turn-signals":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Used to set up confirmation of door locking using the indicators.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>5</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Locking/Unlocking Optical Confirmation (Turn Signal) active”.</em><em><br/></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte5-90daaa01.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-electronic-differential-lock-xds":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the electronic differential lock (XDS).  </p>\n<p>The electronic differential lock (XDS) is an extension of the well-known EDS function. However, XDS does not react to acceleration slip, but rather relieves pressure on the inside front wheel when cornering. XDS applies pressure to the inside wheel during cornering from the hydraulic ESP to prevent slippage.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><em>Byte 17 : </em><br/><em>Bit 3: Tick “(Extended) Electronic Differential Lock (XDS – PR-UG3/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 XDS setting.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10 </strong>”.</p>\n<p>Channel 36 (Electronic Differential Lock (XDS) in drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” <br/>2 “high  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/xdsg6-567d8998.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-enable-bluetooth-audio-a2dp":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Enables Bluetooth audio (A2DP).  </p>\n<p>You can listen to music from your A2DP-compatible phone or mp3 player.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“77 – Telephone</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong> “Coding – 07”</strong> then<strong> “Long Coding Helper”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– <em>Byte <strong>4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0: </strong> Uncheck <strong>“Multimedia Function (Bluetooth Audio) inactive”.</strong></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/D836B768-D607-4E70-92E6-06200694DE00-4d4d00be.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Emergency Flashing<em>(Turn Signals) active </em>” (to activate turn signals)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Tick “Emergency Brake Flashing (Brake Light) active” (to activate brake lights)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte12-2c0d5984.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-fog-lamps-with-high-beam":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> This feature prevents the fog lights from turning off when you turn on your high beams; they will not turn off when you turn on your high beams.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte<strong> 14</strong>: Clear Bit <strong>2</strong><em> </em>: “<em>Fog lights inactive while high beams are on</em>“</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/antibrouillardpleinphareg6-b0c5522b.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-hill-hold-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: Enables </strong>Hill Hold Control (Hill Start Assist).  </p>\n<p>Hill Hold Control maintains brake pressure for a few seconds after the brake pedal is held down for an extended period.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Hill Hold Control (HHC/PR-UG1/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: Hill Hold Control Settings.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p>Select <strong>Channel 58</strong> (Hill Hold Control (HHC) from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Select a value:<br/>0 “normal”<br/>1 “earlier” (restarts with lower acceleration)<br/>2 “later” (restarts with higher acceleration)</p>","beetle-5c-lock-the-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-the-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the RNS 510’s CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 43</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(CD/DVD Ejection Lock active)</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates needle sweep when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)   </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Only compatible with models since 2012 </strong>(Compatible module: 6R0 920 860 K)  <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>If the previous method doesn’t work, try this one.</strong><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>10-Adaptation</strong> </p>\n<p>Select “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” from the value list</p>\n<p><em>Select “<strong>On”</strong> in the second value list</em></p>","beetle-5c-park-assist-beep-frequency-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to adjust the frequency of the rear beeps during parking assistance.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “10-Parking<strong>Assistance.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on<strong> “Adaptation – 10” </strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>“Speaker frequency for rear parking aid</em> ” from the drop-down list<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><em>Select</em>a frequency from <em>Stage 1</em> (Low) to <em>Stage 9</em> (High) from the second drop-down list</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0_Module10_Adaptation_speaker-frequency_for_rear-a3ec7081.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-programming-a-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.<br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Ignition Authorization)</strong>, you cannot program a new remote control using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the process.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>7 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 7 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong>“Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/programmertelecommande-51bf4068.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-resetting-the-remote-controls":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle. </p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong><br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Start Authorization)</strong>, you cannot delete the remote controls using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-retrofit-heated-mirrors":"<p><strong>Function</strong>: Turns on the heated and defrosting side mirrors.  </p>\n<p>The vehicle must be equipped with heated side mirrors. Or, for the installation of heated side mirrors (retrofit)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “Long Coding Helper” :</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears,</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 3</strong>: Check “Mirror Heating ON while rear Window Heater ON”<br/>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Heated Outside Mirrors installed”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte15-1c45d71d.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-selective-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose: Allows </strong>you to configure selective door unlocking. <br/></p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Selective Central Locking (Single Door Locking) active”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6R0-937-088-B_Module09_Byte0-87553eca.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-speed-limit-display-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to display the speed limit on the RNS 510 navigation screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”. Then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong><br/>Activate Bit <strong>2</strong>: Speed Threshold for Destination Input active</p>\n<p>+ use voice command to activate Bit 3: Speed Threshold for Speech Destination Input active</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510speed-9dcbaa67.webp\"/></figure>","beetle-5c-tear-wiping":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the windshield wipers once more after using the windshield washer, in order to remove any remaining water from the windshield.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07”</strong> then <strong>“Long Coding Helper”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>14</strong>, <br/>Bit <strong>4</strong>, Check <strong>“Tear Wiping Active”</strong>.</p>","beettle-5c-enable-usb-port-for-iphone-carplay-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the USB port for iPhone CarPlay accounting (after activating App Connect and changing the USB and/or USB cable) for Discover MIB2 PQ (2015/2016). (Retrofit) </p>\n<p>For firmware references: <br/>MST2_EU_VW_PQ_P02XXT</p>\n<p>Modify the MIB2 coding and adaptation to recognize the new USB port (USB connector ref 5Q0 035 726 E) for both CarPlay and USB multimedia playback. A coding pin on the connector needs to be modified.  </p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/app-connect-carplay-activation\">–&gt; App Connect Activation for CarPlay and Android Auto</a><br/><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">–&gt; USB/AUX Port for VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E on VAG Custom</a></strong><br/><a href=\"#/vw/beetle-5c/beetle-5c-deactivate-mirrorlink\"><strong>–&gt; Disable MirrorLink</strong></a><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Assistant Codage Long</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5 </strong>– Select byte<strong>“19</strong>“<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“6-7</strong>” (C0 USB Configuration: USB and iPhone Functionality)<br/><br/><strong>Ligne 2 <strong>(optional)</strong> :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Interface for external media activation – connection 1</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value “<strong><strong>activated</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><br/></p>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/activation-app-connect-pour-volkswagen/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activation APP CONNECT pour Volkswagen</a></blockquote>\n</figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Prise USB / AUX VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E</a></blockquote>\n</figure>"};
